{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a2807aab4fd4622e","status":"completed","result":"139:## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n140-<!-- FILL: Write each open question as one line. Write `None` when nothing blocks. GOOD: Does a missing `--keep` value delete every archive? Decision: no, a missing value exits 2. WEAK: Edge cases are unclear. -->\n141-\n142-1. Where are a packet's problem, purpose and user need written today, per level and for a phase parent, and which of those places is required and validated?\n143-2. For each hop surface, what does it read and what does it emit, and does the purpose travel? Surfaces: the Claude compaction hooks (`runtime/hooks/claude/compact-inject.ts`, `session-prime.ts`) and their counterparts for other runtimes under `runtime/hooks/`, `/speckit:resume`, `/speckit:handoff` and the session relaunch, `/speckit:save` with `generate-context.js`, the deep-loop iteration prompts and child-dispatch briefs.\n144-3. In real packets under `specs/` that have a `handover.md` or several continuity saves, is the purpose restated, shortened or absent? Do phase children restate the parent's purpose or drift from it?\n145-4. Which candidate change closes the measured gap at the lowest cost? The operator's candidates, to be tested and not assumed: acceptance criteria at the parent spec level, a user story or purpose and problem section at the parent level and an improved parent-specific spec template. Add any other candidate the evidence supports, for example a purpose field in the continuity block or in the compaction brief.\n146-5. What is ruled out, and why?\n147-\n148-### Research Context\n149-\n150-Deep research runs against this packet with `/deep:research`, and `research/research.md` is the canonical findings source.\n151-<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n152-\n153----\n154-\n155-\n"}
