{"type":"thinking","text":"Now I understand the flow. I need to:\n\nphase_init:\n1. mkdir -p lineages/deepseek-2/{prompts,iterations,deltas}\n2. Create config in lineage dir (from template + populated fields, sessionId = provided).\n3. Append deep_research.run_initialized through gateway (this writes state log projection in lineage).\n4. Create strategy.md in lineage dir with 5 key questions.\n5. Create findings-registry.json.\n\nphase_main_loop: 5 iterations. For each:\n- read state (config, state log, strategy)\n- determine focus\n- research (read files) — this is the bulk: answer 5 questions\n- write iterations/iteration-NNN.md + deltas/iter-NNN.jsonl\n- gateway append with iteration record\n- run reduce-state.cjs with spec_folder arg and --artifact-dir lineage.\n\nphase_synthesis:\n- write research.md\n- synthesis closeout / terminal record with stopReason maxIterationsReached.\n\nLet me check reduce-state.cjs usage to see args and what it writes. And check the synthesis-closeout script. Also check gateway requirements (stable identity, event types).\n\nImportant: The gateway run-directory = lineage dir. The reducer must be run with --artifact-dir lineage so it writes into lineage (strategy/registry/dashboard). Good.\n\nLet me check whether reduce-state requires config in artifact-dir. Also whether it needs the root spec research dir. Let me read key parts of the reducer CLI."}
