{"type":"thinking","text":"The ledger already has an audit frame from the fanout effect writer (authorization decision). Our gateway appends will chain from sequence 1. Good.\n\nNow, phase_init. Let me create directories and config. Then run the gateway for run_initialized.\n\nPlan for the config in lineage:\n- Use the spec-level config? The YAML says create from template with populate. I'll copy the spec-level config (which already has fanout and topic) but adjust:\n  - lineage.sessionId = fanout-deepseek-2-1794603759690-pm09h3\n  - lineage.parentSessionId = dr-1794603751398 (parent run session) — the fanout-run may want that. Hmm \"lineageId\" in gateway = parentSessionId || sessionId. The prompt pack says runId/sessionId/lineageId all set to the run's session id. But the upcaster's hasStableIdentity accepts runId/sessionId and lineageId/parentSessionId/sessionId. If parentSessionId is set to dr-..., then lineageId would be derived... but we pass lineageId explicitly = session id. Fine.\n  - lineage.lineageMode: \"new\" (since this is a fresh lineage segment, not a resume). The dispatcher said lineageMode new/resume/restart; fan-out lineage is its own run. I'll use \"new\".\n  - lineage.generation: 1\n  - status: initialized\n  - createdAt: now\n  - maxIterations: 5, convergenceThreshold 0.05, stopPolicy max-iterations, antiConvergence.convergenceMode \"default\", minIterations 3.\n  - progressiveSynthesis true.\n  - resource_map.emit true? Spec folder has resource-map.md? Let me check. The spec folder listing didn't show resource-map.md. So resource_map_present false. I'll set false.\n  - executor: kind cli-deepseek-harness, model deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, reasoningEffort max, sandboxMode workspace-write, timeoutSeconds 1800. This matches invocation-metadata and helps provenance.\n  - fanout? The fanout-run config field `fanout` in the spec-level config is the parent. For the lineage config, including `fanout` would confuse reducers (config.fanout present => fan-out mode). In this lineage run, \"phase_synthesis step skip_when config.fanout is present\" — for the lineage, we're running synthesis ourselves. If config.fanout is present, fanout merge is skipped (since we're within a lineage). I'd rather not include fanout in the lineage config — it's a single lineage and the reduce step and synthesis are executed by me. But the YAML's `step_fanout_spawn` is already satisfied by the outer dispatcher.\n\nHmm, does the final lineage config need something to mark it as a lineage? Perhaps `fanout_lineage: {label: \"deepseek-2\", parentArtifactDir: ...}`. Not necessary; keep it clean.\n\nImportant: reduce-state might resolve artifacts relative to config.specFolder. We'll pass --artifact-dir lineage.\n\nLet me check what reduce-state expects for config reading and where it writes if artifactDir is given. Let me grep reduce-state for `artifactDir` usage and `readResearchConfig`."}
