{"type":"tool_result","callId":"call_88b25dc4dd364a809ea8cdbc","status":"completed","result":"35:│   ├── spec.md.tmpl\n50:│   ├── phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl\n51:│   ├── research.spec.md.tmpl\n53:│   └── review.spec.md.tmpl\n114:| Shape | Direct child of a track root, name not `NNN-*`, no `spec.md` |\n119:Numbering continues per folder, so each sub-track numbers its own packets from `001`. One level is supported: a sub-track holds numbered packets, not another sub-track. A declared folder that contains `spec.md` gets the diagnostic `declared folder has spec.md and cannot be a sub-track`, and `create.sh` refuses it.\n158:### Level 1 (< 100 LOC)\n163:├── spec.md                    # Problem statement, goals, scope\n173:### Level 2 (100-499 LOC)\n178:├── spec.md\n191:### Level 3 (≥ 500 LOC)\n196:├── spec.md\n267:├── spec.md\n271:│   ├── spec.md\n284:    ├── spec.md\n338:### Simple Feature (Level 1)\n342:├── spec.md\n348:### Medium Feature (Level 2)\n352:├── spec.md\n363:### Complex Feature (Level 3)\n367:├── spec.md\n386:│   ├── spec.md\n390:│   ├── spec.md\n395:    ├── spec.md\n401:├── spec.md                          <- Phase map + current tree truth\n416:│   ├── spec.md\n422:│   │   ├── spec.md\n"}
