{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-97b3f6848c43c8a3","status":"completed","result":"\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: goal | v2.2 -->\n<!-- HVR_REFERENCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md -->\n<!-- GOAL_AUTHORING: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-goal/SKILL.md -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:directive -->\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n<!-- FILL: Write one sentence: what the packet is for, not how. GOOD: Keep only the newest n archives on request. WEAK: Improve the script. -->\n\n**Objective:** [One sentence. What this packet is for. Not how, not progress.]\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | [The decision, stated so a reader can tell whether work honors it] |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:directive -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- IF level:phase -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:binding -->\n## 2. BINDING\n<!-- FILL: List each child phase and its goal path. Name the precedence rule. GOOD: 001 and 002. Decisions here outrank child detail. WEAK: Children are bound. -->\n\n**Read the child goal before working a phase.** Each is authoritative for its\nphase and binds as if written here.\n\n| Phase | Goal document |\n|-------|---------------|\n| [NNN-phase-slug] | `[NNN-phase-slug]/goal.md` |\n\n**Precedence.** Decisions above outrank child detail. Child detail outranks any\nsummary of it. Name a conflict rather than resolving it silently.\n\n**Stop.** Only the criteria below decide done. An evaluator sees the objective\nstring, not these files.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:binding -->\n\n---\n<!-- /IF -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one command-checkable criterion per line. GOOD: `--keep 3` leaves 3 archives in `logs/archive` and exits 0. WEAK: The work is done. -->\n\n=== AC 35-100\n> every row below is `Met`, `Waived` or `Superseded`. A `Waived` or `Superseded`\n> row MUST name an ADR that exists in `decision-record.md`.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n<!-- FILL: Fill the packet id, the level, the status and the date. GOOD: `004-rotate-logs-keep`. Level 1. Draft. 2026-10-24. WEAK: Packet TBD. -->\n\n**Packet:** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: PACKET-ID]\n**Level:** [2/3/3+]\n**Status:** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Draft/In Progress/Complete]\n**Date:** [YYYY-MM-DD]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:criteria -->\n## 2. CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one row per requirement. The Then clause names a command. GOOD: AC-001: When `--keep 3` runs, Then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3. WEAK: The feature works. -->\n\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: context], When [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: action], Then [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: observable outcome] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: command, file:line, or artifact that proves it] | Unmet | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n| `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n| `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n\n### Waiver cell\n\nWrite `-` when the row is `Met` or `Unmet`. Write `ADR-NNN` when the row is\n`Waived` or `Superseded`, naming a decision record that exists in\n`decision-record.md`. A waiver naming an ADR that is not there fails validation:\nthe point of a waiver is that someone recorded the reasoning, so an unbacked\nwaiver is treated as an unmet criterion rather than as a pass.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:closure -->\n## 3. CLOSURE STATEMENT\n<!-- FILL: Write Yes or No and one sentence. Name a criterion by its id only when it blocks closure. Never write a count of criteria or an id range, because every added row makes it wrong. GOOD: No. AC-002 is unmet. WEAK: All eight criteria AC-001 to AC-008 are met. -->\n\n**Closeable:** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n\n[One sentence: what decides closure now. Name a criterion by id only when it blocks closure.]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:closure -->\n<!-- /IF -->\n"}
