{"type":"thinking","text":"Excellent: Rule 7 — v2.3+ documents fail with required anchor missing. And rule 1: phase parent is exempt because lean document set passes without anchor checks. So a phase parent's spec.md is NOT anchor-validated (exempt), meaning its root purpose section can be missing without failing validation. That's key evidence for Q1: purpose is required at normal levels (via ANCHORS_VALID v2.3+ required anchors) but not at phase-parent level.\n\nWait, but does the phase-parent template stamp v2.2? Yes `<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: phase-parent-spec | v2.2 -->`. So v2.2 → integrity-only, no required sections. Plus the rule says phase parent exempt.\n\nAlso need to check \"problem\" required anchor for level 1/2/3 templates (the test says level 2 has required anchors including problem). And the L1 template? requiredAnchors for level 2 listed problem. Good.\n\nAlso need: description.json `description` one-line is required? Check validation rules for description.json. And graph-metadata. Let me now also check where the \"user need\" concept appears. Search for \"user need\" / \"whom it serves\" across the repo.\n\nLet me move to iteration 1 research properly and gather 3-5 actions with citations. I've done multiple already; budget in the persona counts roughly. I need to be efficient. Let me do targeted greps:\n\n1. `problem` required anchors: confirmed via validation-rules.md:446 (rule 7) and template-structure.js. I should cite source lines. Let me get exact line numbers for template-structure.js requiredAnchors derivation and validation-rules.md.\n2. Phase parent: phase-definitions.md §3 lean trio, phase-parent template \"REQUIRED content ... Root purpose\" and \"Phase-parent note\". Get line numbers.\n3. Description.json: where required/validated.\n4. User need: search.\n\nLet me run a batch of greps with line numbers."}
