{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-8a023a27f5a44bcd","status":"completed","result":"35:  REQUIRED content (MUST author at phase-parent level):\n36:    - Root purpose: what problem does this entire phased decomposition solve?\n65:### Problem Statement\n68:### Purpose\n71:> **Phase-parent note:** This spec.md is the ONLY authored document at the parent level. All detailed planning, task breakdowns, checklists, and decisions live in the child phase folders listed in the Phase Documentation Map below. This keeps the parent from drifting stale as phases execute and pivot.\n=== lean trio\n8:  - \"lean trio policy\"\n80:Create the series parent at the second packet, not later, so each child's commit history stays on one path for as long as possible. Its slug names the artifact, for example `041-write-recipe-fixes`, and its `spec.md` names the artifact and the condition that closes the series. It keeps the lean trio plus an optional `timeline.md` and gets no `goal.md` by default.\n144:### Parent Folder Structure (lean trio policy)\n146:- **Lean trio:** A phase parent only requires **the lean trio** at the parent level: `spec.md`, `description.json`, `graph-metadata.json`.\n=== level req\n163:├── spec.md                    # Problem statement, goals, scope\n=== anchors rule\n443:1. **Scope:** the check reads the level's spec docs whose own template defines anchors. A document whose template ships no anchors is skipped, so an anchored surface is never demanded of a document that never had one. `research/research.md` and `review/review-report.md` are skipped as free-form workflow artifacts, and a phase parent is exempt because its lean document set passes without anchor checks.\n449:7. **A v2.3 document keeps its required sections.** A document whose `SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE` stamp reads v2.3 or later fails with `required anchor '<id>' is missing` for each anchor its rendered template requires and the document lacks; the finding names the `## <heading>` to restore. Sections under an `L2:`, `L3:`, `L3+:` or `FIX ADDENDUM:` heading are optional, and `decision-record.md` requires none because its ADR sections are named by the author. A document stamped v2.2 or earlier, or unstamped, keeps the integrity-only check.\n"}
