{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a5e039caf28a4b9a","status":"completed","result":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/retrieval/session-recovery-spec-kit-resume.md:49:7. Verify the final recovery response includes actionable state and next steps, then routes appropriately to continued `/speckit:resume` work or to a direct read of `implementation-summary.md`, plus its `changelog/` when an older packet still has one, depending on user need\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review/001-research-egm-checks-and-chat-path-gaps/research_archive/2026-11-11T20-11-35Z/iterations/iteration-004.md:49:| 4 | Templates + `validate.sh` | templates ~49.6 KB at Level 1; validator 42 rules, decides nothing a reader must judge | runtime-independent — shell and node, no rule-file budget, no truncation, no loader | runs anywhere a shell runs, no user needed |\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/research/lineages/deepseek-2/containment/baseline/specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/implementation-summary.md:54:When the run finishes, you get `research/research.md`, which says where a packet's problem, purpose and user need drop on each hop and names one change that keeps them. A later packet plans and builds that change.\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/research/lineages/deepseek-2/containment/baseline/specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/tasks.md:48:- [ ] T003 [P] Answer Q1, where the problem, purpose and user need are written per level and for a phase parent, and which places are required and validated (`R`). Verify: the Q1 answer in `R` cites each template and validator rule as `[SOURCE: path:line]`.\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/research/lineages/deepseek-2/containment/baseline/specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/spec.md:3:description: \"A packet keeps its mechanics across relaunch hops and compactions but loses why the work exists and whom it serves. This research packet finds where the purpose drops and names the smallest change that keeps it.\"\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/research/lineages/deepseek-2/containment/baseline/specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/spec.md:36:The operator reported on 2026-11-13 that the core reason, problem, purpose or user need behind a piece of work gets lost after several in-session handovers (relaunch hops) or context compactions. The session keeps the mechanics, such as files, commits and the next action, and loses why the work exists and whom it serves.\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/research/lineages/deepseek-2/containment/baseline/specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/spec.md:48:Find where a packet's problem, purpose and user need are dropped on each hop, and name the smallest change to system-spec-kit logic or templates that keeps them in front of the next session.\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/research/lineages/deepseek-2/containment/baseline/specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/spec.md:142:1. Where are a packet's problem, purpose and user need written today, per level and for a phase parent, and which of those places is required and validated?\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/research/lineages/deepseek-2/deep-research-strategy.md:31:Where a spec packet's problem, purpose and user need are dropped across session 