{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-99c0481dc786fff0","status":"completed","result":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:68:| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:337:A doc with an older stamp, or none, keeps the ERROR it always had, and Draft changes nothing for it. The orchestrator reads every authored doc that is present. The shell mirror reads `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `decision-record.md`, and it adds `acceptance-criteria.md`, `implementation-summary.md` and `goal.md` only when they carry the stamp. A warning never fails `--strict`. The status word must be exactly Draft, so Planned, In Progress and Complete all count as any other value.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:817:**Description:** A packet `goal.md` carries the directive an operator sets as the session objective. Every runtime goal surface caps what it holds and truncates at the tail, where the completion criteria live, so the slice that gets set has a budget.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:834:On a phase parent the `binding` anchor lists each child's goal document. Every row's path must exist on disk. A row naming a child `goal.md` that was never authored is an error: the parent promises a directive the child cannot supply.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:838:❌ **Fail:** a parent `goal.md` whose slice measures 4,120 characters.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:841:SPECDOC_SUFFICIENCY_005: goal.md: durable slice is 4120 characters (> 4000). Cut it in the order section 3 of sk-create-goal's references/budget-and-handoff.md gives, and never drop a criterion.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:846:❌ **Fail:** a binding row `| 003-runtime | \\`003-runtime/goal.md\\` |` when that file is absent.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:849:SPECDOC_SUFFICIENCY_006: goal.md: binding row names '003-runtime/goal.md' which does not exist inside the packet. Author the child goal and its row with /create:goal <parent> phase-add, or child when the folder already exists.\n=== desc\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:226:| **Phase Parent** | `spec.md`, `description.json`, `graph-metadata.json` (lean trio only; heavy docs live in phase children, except an optional `decision-record.md` for decisions that span the phases) |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:228:> **Phase Parent Mode:** A spec folder is treated as a phase parent when at least one direct child matches `^[0-9]{3}-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$` AND that child has `spec.md` OR `description.json`. Detection is implemented identically by `is_phase_parent()` (shell, in `runtime/cli/lib/shell-common.sh`) and `isPhaseParent()` (ESM JS, at `runtime/cli/dist/spec/is-phase-parent.js`). When detected, FILE_EXISTS skips Level-N file requirements at the parent and accepts only the lean trio. Phase children continue to follow their own Level 1/2/3/3+ contract. Tolerant policy: legacy phase parents that retain heavy docs continue to validate without churn.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:875:A Draft packet can repair its own generated metadata instead of failing on it. When a `validate.sh --strict` run finds that every error comes from a derived-metadata rule that `repair-derived.cjs` can fix, it runs `repair-derived.cjs --folder <packet> --apply` once, prints each file it rewrote, and validates again. The repair rewrites generated metadata (`description.json`, `graph-metadata.json`), frontmatter packet pointers and the Spec Folder row, and never any other body text.\n"}
