{"type":"thinking","text":"Good. The save writes continuity into the leaf's implementation-summary.md, not the parent (phase parent descends into leaf) — so a parent's purpose isn't written by save at all. For a research record, save writes into spec.md? Hmm, \"or a research record's spec.md\" — perhaps research packets route continuity to spec.md. But the 006 packet has implementation-summary.md at its root.\n\nI have enough for iteration 1. But Q1 needs \"per level\": Level 1 spec.md problem section; Level 2/3 same plus AC; phase parent lean trio + template requires root purpose but validator exempt. And which are required AND validated:\n- Level 1: spec.md required (FILE_EXISTS; core doc list). Problem anchor required for v2.3+ docs by ANCHORS_VALID rule 7. But is the problem anchor's CONTENT validated? No — ANCHORS_VALID only checks presence, not content. PLACEHOLDER_FILLED checks unfilled template tokens. So \"problem statement present\" is required structurally, not semantically.\n- description.json is required at all levels including phase parent (FILE_EXISTS), and its `description` field is generated/validated? Derived metadata rule. Let me check DESCRIPTION_* rules. Actually rule 875 says repair-derived rewrites description.json. Let me grep for \"description.json\" validation sections (maybe DERIVED_METADATA).\n\nLet me quickly check validation-rules for the metadata rule name."}
