{"type":"thinking","text":"Great. Q1 evidence is solid:\n- Level 1/2/3: problem/purpose lives in spec.md §2 PROBLEM & PURPOSE, anchor `problem`, required (ANCHORS_VALID rule 7 for v2.3+ docs; core spec template v2.4) and file required (FILE_EXISTS).\n- Validation checks presence of anchor/heading, not semantic content (ANCHORS_VALID rules 4-7; PLACEHOLDER_FILLED only checks tokens).\n- Phase parent: lean trio required (spec.md, description.json, graph-metadata.json); phase-parent template requires root purpose (lines 35-37) with Problem Statement/Purpose (65-68) BUT phase parents are exempt from anchor checks (validation-rules:443) and the phase-parent template stamp is v2.2 (so rule 7 doesn't apply). So purpose at parent is authoring convention, not validated.\n- description.json `description` is a candidate carrier (one-line) at parent level; required file, but its content is short and derived. Need to verify description.json field validation — but enough to say it's required as a file, and `description` is a one-line summary.\n- goal.md: carries Durable Directive \"what this packet is for\" but optional (not in required files; create-goal authors it). Need to confirm goal.md is not required. It's not in FILE_EXISTS table. And SPECDOC_SUFFICIENCY applies only if present. Good.\n\nNow write iteration 1 file + delta + gateway + reduce. Then iteration 2 etc.\n\nBut note the \"Findings\" need to be one per line and each cited. Let me define findings for iteration 1:\n\n1. Problem/purpose for standard packets is authored once in spec.md §2 with `problem` anchor; required structurally for v2.3+ docs. [SOURCE: templates/core/spec.md.tmpl:100-112; validation-rules.md:449]\n2. For Level 1 the required file list includes spec.md; Level 2 adds acceptance-criteria; Level 3 adds decision-record as lazy add-on. [validation-rules.md:218-223]\n3. Phase parent required docs are lean trio only; purpose isn't in the trio's required content. [phase-definitions.md:144-146; validation-rules.md:228]\n4. Phase-parent template REQUIRES root purpose authoring, but phase parent is exempt from anchor checks and its template is stamped v2.2, so no validator enforces it. [phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl:35-37,65-68,80; validation-rules.md:443,449]\n5. No template or validator names \"user need\"; the nearest carriers are Purpose (one sentence) and description.json's one-line description. [grep evidence: spec.md.tmpl:98-106? description.json fields] — Cite description.json produced by repair-derived (description, keywords) and spec.md.tmpl Purpose.\n\nWait, for \"user need\" I should cite absence honestly as [INFERENCE: based on grep across templates... with no hits]. The source consulted list can name the grep. Better: finding says \"No template carries a user-need field; the purpose line is the only place a user need can be stated\" [INFERENCE: based on X and Y].\n\n6. goal.md Durable Directive is a purpose carrier but optional and not part of required files; not in FILE_EXISTS. [goal.md.tmpl:38-41; validation-rules.md:218-223] \n7. continuity block has no purpose field (thin-continuity-record.ts:60-73) — that's Q2 but also Q1 \"where written today\". Good.\n\nNow write the iteration file. Keep it focused. Then delta JSONL with iteration record + finding rows. Must include `sources` array per finding.\n\nnewInfoRatio: all 6 new? Some partial. I'd say 6 findings: 5 fully new, 1 partially (user-need absence). Ratio = (5 + 0.5)/6 = 0.917. That's high but honest for iteration 1.\n\nFindingsCount = 6.\n\nThen gateway record with required fields: type iteration, runId/sessionId/lineageId, mode, target_agent, agent_definition_loaded, resolved_route, newInfoRatio, status, focus, findingsCount, noveltyJustification, keyQuestions, answeredQuestions (exact text of Q1), ruledOut, toolsUsed, sourcesQueried, timestamp, durationMs, graphEvents, run.\n\nNote answeredQuestions must match strategy's `- [ ]` text exactly. Q1 text: \"Where are a packet's problem, purpose and user need written today, per level and for a phase parent, and which of those places is required and validated?\" — I have it exactly.\n\nWill the reducer tick the box? It says exact match. Good.\n\nLet me write iteration-001.md."}
