dation/validation-rules.md:212-228,443,449\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/continuity/thin-continuity-record.ts:60-73\",\"specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/description.json:2-9\",\"specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/spec.md:36\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-13T21:09:00.000Z\",\"durationMs\":300000,\"graphEvents\":[]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-001\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"label\":\"The only authored purpose carrier for a standard packet is spec.md section 2 PROBLEM & PURPOSE, holding a Problem Statement and a one-sentence Purpose; the core template ships the problem anchor and Level 2 requires it.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/spec.md.tmpl:100-112\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/template-structure.vitest.ts:74-83\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-002\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"label\":\"The problem anchor is enforced only as structural presence: a v2.3+ SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE stamp fails on a missing required anchor, while v2.2 or unstamped documents keep integrity-only checking and content is never graded.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:449\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:57\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-003\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"label\":\"File requirements rise with level while the purpose carrier stays one section: Level 1 requires spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md and implementation-summary.md; Level 2 adds acceptance-criteria.md; Level 3 keeps that set with decision-record.md as a lazy add-on.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:218-223\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-004\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"label\":\"A phase parent is validated against the lean trio spec.md, description.json and graph-metadata.json only, so it has exactly one prose document in which purpose could live.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md:144-146\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:226-228\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-005\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"label\":\"The phase-parent spec template demands root purpose as REQUIRED parent content and provides Problem Statement and Purpose subsections, noting this spec is the only authored parent document.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/packet-types/phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl:35-37\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/packet-types/phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl:65-71\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-006\",\"severity\":\"P0\",\"label\":\"The phase-parent purpose requirement is unvalidated: phase parents are exempt from anchor checks and the phase-parent template is stamped v2.2, so a parent can ship an empty Problem & Purpose and still pass strict validation.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:443\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/packet-types/phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl:80\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-007\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"label\":\"Two secondary purpose carriers exist but neither is required: goal.md's Durable Directive asks what the packet is for yet goal.md is absent from required files, and description.json's one-line description is the only purpose-shaped field present at every level.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/addons/goal.md.tmpl:38-41\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:218-228\",\"specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/description.json:2-9\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-008\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"label\":\"No template or validator surface uses the term user need; the phrase appears only in packet 006 itself, leaving the one-sentence Purpose and the one-line description.json description as the nearest authored slots.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/spec.md:36\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-009\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"label\":\"The continuity record every save writes has no purpose field: its fields are packet_pointer, timestamps, recent_action, next_safe_action, blockers, key_files, completion_pct and question ids, and next_safe_action is an action rather than a reason.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/continuity/thin-continuity-record.ts:60-73\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Searching for a dedicated user-need template\",\"reason\":\"No template or validator surface uses the term; the answer must name the nearest existing carrier instead.\",\"iteration\":1}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Treating acceptance-criteria.md as a purpose carrier\",\"reason\":\"Its sections are METADATA, CRITERIA and CLOSURE STATEMENT, so it measures completion and carries no why.\",\"iteration\":1}","file_path":"deltas/iter-001.jsonl"}}
