{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-b4f7b9e2f8ab331e","status":"completed","result":"---\ntitle: \"Session Handover: DeepSeek Harness follow-up for the v4.0.2.0 release\"\ndescription: \"The DeepSeek Harness mode is built and committed. This session's later work is uncommitted: the verified LLM Gateway route, four dispatch-rule fixes, a readability pass and a re-mint. A release session commits it and corrects the v4.0.2.0 changelogs, which still say no keyed run exists.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deepseek harness release handover\"\n  - \"dsh release v4.0.2.0\"\n  - \"cli-deepseek-harness commit follow-up\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n# Session Handover: DeepSeek Harness follow-up for the v4.0.2.0 release\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: handover | v1.0 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:handover-summary -->\n## 1. Handover Summary\n\nThe `cli-deepseek-harness` mode shipped in commits `602309b436` to `8df2e4c343`, already on `origin/main`. This session's later work sits uncommitted in the working tree: the LLM Gateway route verified live, four dispatch-rule fixes, a documentation readability pass and a compiled-routing re-mint. Start at section 3.1: commit the files in section 2.3, then correct the three changelogs that still say no keyed run exists.\n\n- **From Session:** 2026-11-05 to 2026-11-06, the overnight `/goal` session on `main`\n- **To Session:** the release session that cuts `v4.0.2.0` (latest tag is `v4.0.1.0`)\n- **Phase Completed:** IMPLEMENTATION and verification. Nothing in this handover is committed\n- **Handover Time:** 2026-11-06\n- **Recent action**: final gate run 5 green; recursive strict validation `RESULT: PASSED` on 15 of 15 folders\n<!-- /ANCHOR:handover-summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:context-transfer -->\n## 2. Context Transfer\n\n### 2.1 Key Decisions Made\n| Decision | Rationale | Impact |\n| -------- | --------- | ------ |\n| LLM Gateway `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` promoted to verified | Keyed run 2026-11-06: exit 0, `final.reason.kind` `completed`, empty stderr. One `fanout-run.cjs` lineage completed with a clean containment scan | `executor-config.ts`, `live-contracts.json` (already committed); docs in section 2.3 |\n| OpenCode Go stays \"configured, not verified\" | `OPENCODE_API_KEY` is unset, so no keyed request was sent. It stays out of default allowlists | Playbook scenario for OpenCode Go records `SKIP` |\n| `$REPO` resolves to the checkout in `no-repo-root-dotenv` and `dsh-home-isolated` | Before the fix, `cd \"$REPO\"` and `DSH_HOME=$REPO/x` both passed the rules they should fail. Rejecting every variable would also block the safe `cd \"$W\"` pattern | `dispatch-rule-checks.mjs`, its test file, dispatch README |\n| Thirteenth rule `dsh-availability-required` (check `command-v-dsh-required`) | Every other CLI has a PATH check; dsh had none, and the README claimed a version check the code cannot do | `hard-rules.json`, `dispatch-rule-checks.mjs`, rule-count docs |\n| Six `DSH_*_DIR` overrides listed in `.env.example` | The env-token check failed on them; they are documented folder paths, not secrets | `.env.example` |\n| Research `.dsh-home/` deleted | A dsh session folder from a research lineage was committed by mistake in `602309b436` | 8 deleted files under `001-deep-research/.../lineages/deepseek/.dsh-home/` |\n| No AI Council seat for dsh yet | The 012 ADR-001 reopen condition is now met, but one proven route and an `rc` pin argue for waiting | None; operator may reopen later |\n\n### 2.2 Blockers Encountered\n**Blockers**: none open for the release.\n\n| Blocker | Status | Resolution/Workaround |\n| ------- | ------ | --------------------- |\n| OpenCode Go key unset | Open, not blocking | Release ships the route as \"configured, not verified\" |\n| Dispatch-audit run counted lineage snapshot copies | Resolved | Run vitest with `--exclude '**/containment/baseline/**'`; the real suite is 7 files, 870 tests |\n\n### 2.3 Files Modified\n**Commit these** (all this session's work):\n\n| Area | Paths | Change |\n| ---- | ----- | ------ |\n| Dispatch rules | `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.mjs`, `dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs`, `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/README.md` | `$REPO` alias, new availability rule, 41 checks, README rows corrected |\n| Mode packet | `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-deepseek-harness/` (SKILL.md, ROUTER.md, README.md, hard-rules.json, references, assets, changelog `v1.0.0.0.md`, playbook incl. all 14 `stress/` files) | Thirteen rules, verified-route facts, routing wording narrowed to harness vocabulary, README order, playbook results |\n| Hub | `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/` SKILL.md, ROUTER.md, README.md, `changelog/v1.8.0.0.md`, four `feature-catalog/` files | Stale \"no keyed run\" claims corrected, rule count |\n| Mirrors | `.hermes/skills/cli-deepseek-harness/{SKILL,ROUTER}.md`, `.hermes/skills/cli-external-orchestration/{SKILL,ROUTER}.md` | Regenerated by `sync-skills-hermes.cjs` |\n| Compiled routing | `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/013-live-activation/activation/cli-external-orchestration/manifest.json`, the 8 files under `specs/sk-doc/z_archive/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/` (`009-.../004-cli-external-orchestration/` and `013-live-activation/.../cli-external-orchestration/manifest.json`) | Re-mint 8, `effectivePolicyHash` `72d53d924f68547cef8e0a5a605b55b238cae6f0a8451d406bd6dcc812697b46` |\n| Trigger index | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json` and three files in `runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/` | Rebuilt |\n| Env template | `.env.example` | Six `DSH_*_DIR` lines |\n| Packet | `085-.../goal.md`, `graph-metadata.json`, `handover.md`, `014-.../evidence/final-gate-2026-11-06-r4.txt`, `-r5.txt`, and the 8 `.dsh-home` deletions | LOG rows, evidence |\n\n**Leave out** (other sessions' work, not this packet): everything under `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/003-weak-model-spec-authoring/` and `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/004-decision-capture/`.\n\n### 2.4 Traps & Scar Tissue\n| Trap / blast site | Activation condition | Load-bearing or defensive? | How to avoid re-paying it |\n"}
