{"type":"tool_call","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a02b70510cb4472b","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/371-purpose-retention-research && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport os,re\ndef purpose(path):\n    t=open(path,encoding='utf-8',errors='ignore').read()\n    m=re.search(r'###\\s+Purpose\\s*\\n+(.+?)(?:\\n#|\\n>|\\n---|\\Z)',t,re.S|re.I)\n    return re.sub(r'\\s+',' ',m.group(1)).strip() if m else ''\ndef real(p): return p and 'YOUR_VALUE_HERE' not in p and '[One-sentence' not in p\ndef words(s): return set(re.findall(r'[a-z]{4,}',s.lower()))\nrows=[]\nfor dirpath,dirnames,filenames in os.walk('specs'):\n    if any(x in dirpath for x in ('research_archive','containment','z_archive','node_modules','/scratch')): continue\n    if 'spec.md' not in filenames: continue\n    kids=[d for d in dirnames if re.match(r'^\\d{3}-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$',d) and (os.path.exists(os.path.join(dirpath,d,'spec.md')) or os.path.exists(os.path.join(dirpath,d,'description.json')))]\n    if not kids: continue\n    pp=purpose(os.path.join(dirpath,'spec.md'))\n    if not real(pp): continue\n    for k in kids[:6]:\n        kp=purpose(os.path.join(dirpath,k,'spec.md'))\n        if real(kp):\n            pw,kw=words(pp),words(kp); jac=len(pw&kw)/len(pw|kw) if (pw|kw) else 0\n            rows.append((jac,dirpath,k,pp,kp))\njs=sorted(r[0] for r in rows)\nprint('pairs',len(rows),'median',round(js[len(js)//2],3),'<0.10',sum(1 for j in js if j<0.10),'<=0.00',sum(1 for j in js if j==0))\nrows.sort()\nfor r in rows[:2]+rows[len(rows)//2:len(rows)//2+1]:\n    print('\\nJ=%.2f %s -> %s'%(r[0],r[1],r[2])); print(' P:',r[3][:220]); print(' C:',r[4][:220])\nEOF","description":"Compute overlap distribution on real pairs"}}
{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a02b70510cb4472b","status":"completed","result":"pairs 1029 median 0.067 <0.10 700 <=0.00 125\n\nJ=0.00 specs/agents-md/repo-rule-operations/002-repo-rule-advisor-surfacing -> 005-trigger-coverage-check\n P: Decide, from repository evidence, what should surface repo rules, how to write them shorter without losing what enforces them, and how `AGENTS.md`, Gate 5 or a hook should load them without flooding or poisoning context.\n C: CI fails when a rule's Fires-when bullet has no counterpart in its router row. <!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\nJ=0.00 specs/agents-md/repo-rule-operations/002-repo-rule-advisor-surfacing -> 006-rule-concision-rewrites\n P: Decide, from repository evidence, what should surface repo rules, how to write them shorter without losing what enforces them, and how `AGENTS.md`, Gate 5 or a hook should load them without flooding or poisoning context.\n C: The corpus shrinks by 20% to 28% while every norm, test, exception, Fires-when bullet and self-check item survives, and each cut is listed. <!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\nJ=0.07 specs/system-speckit/memory-search-and-knowledge/002-xce-research-based-refinement/003-advisor-and-codegraph -> 001-causal-traversal-bfs\n P: Own the shared BFS helper so it remains visible as shared infrastructure for both code-graph and skill-advisor consumers. The codegraph-specific nested feature-adoption content moved to `system-code-graph/009-advisor-cod\n C: One shared, snapshot-equivalence-tested BFS traversal helper serves both call sites, removing the recursive-SQL dependency while making the hot read path faster and the dormant memo path effectively free. <!-- /ANCHOR:pr\n"}
