{"type":"thinking","text":"Now iteration 5: Q5 \"What is ruled out, and why?\" plus stress-testing the Q4 recommendation. Since the dispatcher says max-iterations policy and convergence is telemetry only, we do all 5.\n\nFor Q5, I need to consolidate all ruled-out directions with reasons:\n1. Dedicated user-need template/field — no template surface; nearest carrier suffices; adding a new document increases authoring load without a reader.\n2. Accept criteria at parent as a purpose carrier — measures done, no why slot; breaks lean trio; high migration.\n3. Parent-level user story/purpose section as a NEW mechanism — already exists; the gap is content and reader.\n4. Improved parent template alone — no validation/read; insufficient.\n5. Treating handover.md as purpose carrier — template has no slot and 71/96 real handovers omit purpose.\n6. Treating continuity block as purpose carrier today — present but has no purpose field; save target purpose-blind.\n7. Treating compaction Goal facet as purpose — it is next_safe_action.\n8. Treating resume as purpose carrier — no output slot, and spec.md read is contradictory.\n9. Relying on the relaunch note — ephemeral, gitignored, unvalidated; no notes sampled.\n10. Searching for a purpose-content validator — none exists; ANCHORS_VALID presence only, PLACEHOLDER_FILLED tokens only.\n11. Treating the deep-loop research_topic as purpose carrier — free text, not read from spec.md, can be a bare label.\n12. Child restating parent purpose naturally — 0/1029 exact, median 0.067; needs a copy/read mechanism.\n\nThen stress the recommendation (D: purpose field in continuity block):\n- Failure mode 1: writer never populates it → fallback to spec.md read at save time; if missing everywhere, the field stays absent and the Goal facet falls back to next_safe_action (status quo).\n- Failure mode 2: parent purpose itself empty (80/297) → the field would be empty; so D depends on the authoring fix (generator + stamp). That's why the recommendation is a pair.\n- Failure mode 3: phase child save descends to the leaf and reads the parent; if the parent is not the immediate ancestor (nested sub-phase), the walk must climb until a real purpose is found. The pointer walk exists; risk is bounded.\n- Failure mode 4: schema churn / existing records; optional field avoids migration.\n- Failure mode 5: hook budget; the snapshot already renders from the record, so adding one line is cheap.\n- Counter-evidence that would overturn: if writers already have a goal.md on most packets and the handoff note reliably carries goal, D might be redundant. Measured: goal.md presence? Let me count how many packets have goal.md. Also count handover notes? No notes. If goal.md is widespread, then a simpler fix could be to have resume read goal.md. Let me measure goal.md presence.\n\nAlso check: is `goal_packet` in handoff notes useful? No notes exist. So measure goal.md coverage. If goal.md exists in many packets, the cheapest fix might be \"resume reads goal.md directive\" rather than a new continuity field. Let me measure.\n\nLet me also check the goal.md \"Objective\" exact field and whether it's usually filled. And count goal.md."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-9fcbe9425ac0f998","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/371-purpose-retention-research && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport glob,re\ngoals=[f for f in glob.glob('specs/**/goal.md',recursive=True) if not any(x in f for x in ('research_archive','containment','z_archive','node_modules'))]\nspecs=[f for f in glob.glob('specs/**/spec.md',recursive=True) if not any(x in f for x in ('research_archive','containment','z_archive','node_modules'))]\nprint('goal.md files:',len(goals),'spec.md files:',len(specs))\nfilled=0\nfor f in goals:\n    t=open(f,encoding='utf-8',errors='ignore').read()\n    m=re.search(r'\\*\\*Objective:\\*\\*\\s*(.+)',t)\n    if m and 'YOUR_VALUE_HERE' not in m.group(1) and '[One sentence' not in m.group(1): filled+=1\nprint('goal.md with a real Objective:',filled)\nfrac=len(goals)/len(specs)\nprint('goal coverage: %.1f%%'%(frac*100))\nEOF","description":"Measure goal.md coverage and objective fill"}}
