{"type":"thinking","text":"Important counter-evidence: goal.md exists in 920 packets (28.4% of spec.md files), 884 with a real Objective. So for ~28% of packets there is a durable directive that carries \"what the packet is for\". This could be an alternative carrier — and a cheaper fix might be to make resume/compaction read goal.md when present (the relaunch note already sets goal_packet). But 71.6% of packets have no goal.md, so it cannot be the general fix. Also, goal.md's Objective is one sentence and decisions; does it carry user need? Template says \"What this packet is for. Not how, not progress.\" That's purpose, not necessarily user need.\n\nAnd user need: only 333 of 2866 real purposes mention a user/beneficiary — 11.6%. So even where purpose is filled, it rarely names whom it serves. That's a strong finding: the \"user need\" half of the problem is absent even in real purposes. This affects Q4: a purpose field alone may carry the why but not the who. The recommendation should require the field to hold problem + purpose + who, or add a user-need clause. But \"smallest change\" — a single `purpose` field populated from the existing Purpose sentence would carry the why but the who is rare. Could recommend the field hold the Problem & Purpose section (both paragraphs) rather than just Purpose, so the problem (which usually names who) travels. Let me check: do problem statements mention users? Let me measure. If Problem Statement often names a user, then carrying the section is better than the Purpose sentence.\n\nLet me measure beneficiary mentions in Problem Statement."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-8ebf021a7264d5e7","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/371-purpose-retention-research && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport glob,re\nspecs=[f for f in glob.glob('specs/**/spec.md',recursive=True) if not any(x in f for x in ('research_archive','containment','z_archive','node_modules'))]\nreal=0; ben=0\nfor f in specs:\n    t=open(f,encoding='utf-8',errors='ignore').read()\n    m=re.search(r'###\\s+Problem Statement\\s*\\n+(.+?)(?:\\n###|\\n#|\\n---|\\Z)',t,re.S|re.I)\n    if not m: continue\n    p=re.sub(r'\\s+',' ',m.group(1)).strip()\n    if 'YOUR_VALUE_HERE' in p or '[One-paragraph' in p: continue\n    real+=1\n    if re.search(r'\\b(operator|user|users|reader|whom|who)\\b',p,re.I): ben+=1\nprint('real problem statements:',real,'mention a user/beneficiary:',ben)\nEOF","description":"Measure beneficiary mentions in problem statements"}}
