{"type":"thinking","text":"Interesting:\n- Real problem statements: 2884; 623 mention a user/beneficiary (21.6%) — better than Purpose (11.6%) but still low.\n- goal.md Objective overlaps Purpose at median 0.256 (854 pairs), with 132 below 0.10 — meaning goal and purpose often diverge. That's counter-evidence for using goal.md as a purpose proxy: it carries a different (directive) statement, and 844 packets lack it.\n\nThis strengthens the recommendation's design: the continuity field should carry the problem+purpose pair (or a \"why\" line) rather than only Purpose, and it cannot rely on goal.md.\n\nAlso for Q5, additional ruled out: relying on goal.md as the purpose carrier (28.4% coverage, median 0.256 overlap with purpose, so not the same content).\n\nNow, stress test D:\n- If the continuity field is populated from spec.md's Problem & Purpose, and a phase child's own section is local, the writer must climb to the parent. Confirmed the save path already walks parents (updatePhaseParentPointersAfterSave). Risk: nested sub-phases (up to depth limit 4?) and parents with empty purpose (80/297) → depends on authoring fix.\n- If field optional, no migration; but optional fields can be left unwritten. Mitigation: writer always attempts population; fallback chain leaf → ancestor → handoff Goal → absent.\n- Hook budget: the snapshot already exists; one line addition.\n\nCounter-evidence that would overturn D: a cheaper existing surface already read by all hops. Resume reads handover.md first (<24h). If handover.md reliably carried purpose, it would be that surface — but 71/96 omit purpose and the template has no slot. So no existing surface. That confirms D.\n\nNow Q5 findings:\n1. Ruled out: new parent document (AC or new purpose file) — no purpose slot in AC, lean-trio conflict, 297-parent migration.\n2. Ruled out: parent template alone — template already requires, parent exempt + v2.2 + generic generator text.\n3. Ruled out: handover.md as carrier — no slot, 71/96 no purpose vocabulary.\n4. Ruled out: continuity block as-is — present but purpose-blind; no field; save target purpose-blind.\n5. Ruled out: compaction Goal facet — built from next_safe_action.\n6. Ruled out: resume as purpose carrier — no output slot, contradictory spec.md read.\n7. Ruled out: relaunch note — ephemeral gitignored runtime state, no notes, unvalidated.\n8. Ruled out: goal.md as general carrier — 28.4% coverage, median 0.256 overlap with Purpose, directive not problem/why.\n9. Ruled out: validator-only fix — ANCHORS_VALID presence only; PLACEHOLDER_FILLED tokens only; no semantic grading; and a hard rule would fail 80 existing parents unless grandfathered.\n10. Ruled out: relying on natural child restatement — 0/1029 exact, median 0.067.\n11. User need is not carried even by real purposes: only 333/2866 (11.6%) mention a user/beneficiary; problem statements 623/2884 (21.6%). So any purpose field must include the problem statement or a who clause to carry the user need.\n12. Stress test of D: three failure modes and mitigations; the decisive dependency is the authoring fix for parents with empty purpose. If parent purpose is empty, D's fallback must be a visible \"unset\" marker rather than a silent generic line.\n13. Counter-evidence that would overturn D: an existing ubiquitous surface already read by every hop. None found; handover is absent in most packets or lacks purpose, goal.md covers 28.4%, spec.md is read inconsistently. So D stands.\n\nThat's 13 findings; maybe too many but Q5 is the ruling-out question. FindingsCount must match delta rows. Let me do 11 findings to keep it manageable.\n\nnewInfoRatio: new measurements (user-need prevalence, goal.md coverage/overlap) + synthesis. 8 new + 3 partial → (8+1.5)/11=0.86. Use 0.88.\n\nThen after iteration 5: phase_synthesis. Need to:\n- Write research.md with 17-section-ish template? The workflow says compile research.md; the research skill has an assets research.md template? The spec's REQ-001/002/003: answers all five questions with citations, names one recommended change with cost and validation, lists ruled out. So research.md should contain those. There is `templates/addons/research.md.tmpl` (for system-spec-kit research packets), but the deep-research workflow's research.md is a synthesis (the skill says workflow owns it, not create.sh --level research). I'll write a comprehensive synthesis with sections: Executive summary, Method, Q1-Q5 answers, recommendation, ruled out, evidence tables, convergence report, sources.\n\n- Then terminal synthesis record via synthesis-closeout.cjs with --stop-reason maxIterationsReached. The closeout writes a terminal event file(s) that the gateway must append. It also validates the output (research.md) and dashboard. Let me inspect its main to know required inputs and what it checks (finding count, registry, etc.). Let me read the rest of synthesis-closeout main (lines 260-420). Also it may require the dashboard to exist (it does) and research.md to have required sections? Let me check."}
