{"type":"thinking","text":"Everything looks good. But I notice iteration 3's narrative has 9 findings and findingsCount 9 — good. Iteration 4 narrative has 9 findings. Iteration 5 has 11. Fine.\n\nWait: iteration 2 narrative has 10 findings, delta has 10 rows. Iteration 1 has 9. Good.\n\nNow verify citations in research.md: check that all specific `[SOURCE: path:line]` references resolve. Let me write a quick script to extract `[SOURCE: <path>:<line>]` patterns, skip globs, and check file existence and line count >= line. Also check iteration files similarly.\n\nAlso check no writes outside lineage: run git status in repo (read-only). It will show lineage files plus maybe other lineage (deepseek-1) changes made by the sibling process — not mine. I should confirm my own writes are only under deepseek-2. Since I only used write/edit with relative paths in cwd (lineage) and one edit on deep-research-config.json, plus /tmp. The reducer wrote into lineage. Good.\n\nLet me run citation checks and git status."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-b1bc75265dff1846","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/371-purpose-retention-research && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re,os,glob\nroot='/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/371-purpose-retention-research'\nlin='specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/research/lineages/deepseek-2'\nfiles=[os.path.join(lin,'research.md')]+sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(lin,'iterations','iteration-*.md')))\npat=re.compile(r'\\[SOURCE: ([^\\]\\s]+?):(\\d+)(?:[-,](\\d+))?\\]')\nbad=[]; ok=0\nfor f in files:\n    t=open(f,encoding='utf-8',errors='ignore').read()\n    for m in pat.finditer(t):\n        p=m.group(1)\n        if '*' in p or p.startswith('http'): continue\n        full=os.path.join(root,p)\n        if not os.path.exists(full):\n            bad.append((os.path.basename(f),p,'missing')); continue\n        n=sum(1 for _ in open(full,encoding='utf-8',errors='ignore'))\n        last=int(m.group(3) or m.group(2))\n        if last>n: bad.append((os.path.basename(f),p,'line %d > %d'%(last,n)))\n        else: ok+=1\nprint('resolved citations:',ok,'bad:',len(bad))\nfor b in bad[:15]: print(b)\nEOF","description":"Validate cited paths and lines"}}
