y for this target\"\n195-        - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local research archive directory for this target\"\n196-\n197-  step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n198-    description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n199-    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n200-    if_present:\n201-      bind:\n202-        reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n203-    if_absent:\n204-      bind:\n205-        reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n206-\n207-  step_fanout_spawn:\n208-    description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n209-    skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n210-    instructions: |\n211-      Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n212-      isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n213-      fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n214-      deep/research command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n215-      deep-research agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n216-      sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n217-      After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n218-      phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n219-      phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n220-    sub_steps:\n221-      step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n222-        description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n223-        skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n224-        command: |\n225-          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n226-            --spec-folder {spec_folder} \\\n--\n1815:            - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the research yourself, write the iteration file and the delta, and hand the iteration record to the append gateway (append-mode-event.cjs) exactly as the leaf contract requires, never writing the state log yourself, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n1816-            - \"Nested CLI dispatch from a lineage is a route violation, not a slow path: a codex lineage that runs this script spawns codex inside its own sandbox, where the child cannot initialize and every iteration fails. The script refuses that case before any spawn and before any dispatch receipt is written, exiting RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE; that refusal is a route error to fix, never a redispatchable executor failure.\"\n1817-            - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so codex produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard (CODEX_SESSION_ID) + env allowlist (CODEX_/OPENAI_/AZURE_OPENAI_) enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1818-            - \"Fails closed when the codex binary is absent (exit 1) — parity with the fan-out cli-codex lineage guard in fanout-run.cjs; codex routing never degrades to native\"\n1819-            - \"codex exec reads the iteration prompt from stdin via the trailing '-' (input: promptBody); '-c model_reasoning_effort=' maps reasoning depth, default medium; '-c service_tier=' forwarded when configured\"\n1820-            - \"--sandbox workspace-write is required so the iteration can write its own iteration file/delta/state record (read-only would fail the post-dispatch artifact gate); -c approval_policy=never keeps it non-interactive; --model omitted when unset so ~/.codex/config.toml default applies\"\n1821:        post_dispatch_validate:\n1822-          validator: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/post-dispatch-validate.ts#validateIterationOutputs\"\n1823-          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type research --artifact-dir {artifact_dir} --iteration {current_iteration}\"\n1824-          command_note: \"Mechanical leaf-reliability gate: exit 0 = complete; non-zero prints one machine reason (dispatch_failed|iteration_file_missing|state_record_missing|route_proof_missing|route_proof_mismatch|delta_file_missing). dispatch_failed means the narrative is missing and the completion receipt shows a non-zero exit or a signal. The script enforces the artifact + route-proof contract instead of trusting the leaf to self-report, and a non-zero exit triggers on_failure.redispatch_once.\"\n1825-          assert_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1826-          assert_appended: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1827-          assert_jsonl_fields: [type, iteration, newInfoRatio, status, focus, mode]\n1828-          route_proof:\n1829-            mode: research\n1830-            target_agent: deep-research\n1831-            agent_definition_loaded: true\n1832-            resolved_route: \"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\"\n1833-          dispatchReceipt:\n1834-            receiptDir: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts\"\n1835-            dispatchId: \"research-i{current_iteration}-g{config.lineage.generation}\"\n1836-          optional_jsonl_fields:\n1837-            logOffset: \"Byte offset where the seekable log region starts\"\n1838-            logSize: \"Byte length of the seekable log region\"\n1839-            logPath: \"Absolute path to the file containing the seekable log region\"\n1840-            skippedCount: \"Missed fixed-rate slots counted for the completed dispatch; 0 when no slot was missed\"\n1841-            slotDurationMs: \"Monotonic elapsed duration for the completed dispatch slot\"\n1842-          assert_canonical_type: \"iteration\"\n"}
